es, including Source Control, Containerization, Continuous Integration, and Change Management. Manage, prioritise and partially implement the backlog of CI/CD pipeline hardening tasks and security checks integration in close collaboration with Infrastructure and DevOps teams. Identify, assess, and prioritise vulnerabilities in the product, development processes and tools used throughout the CI/CD lifecycle including performing security assessments and using automated scanning tools to detect weaknesses. Developing, managing and implementing remediation plans to fix identified vulnerabilities, ensuring they are resolved promptly. Implement robust access control mechanisms to regulate access to critical information resources. Conduct regular security audits and enhance practices related to secret management, vulnerability management, network segmentation, system hardening, integrity control, incident monitoring, and response in cloud and containerized environments. Provide security training to team members, raising awareness of potential threats and promoting secure architecture and coding practices. Evaluate emerging technologies and security tools to select the most effective solutions for our environment. PERKS AND BENEFITS Join our dynamic product company and experience a recruiting process like no other one that is both timesaving and highly efficient. Why choose us? Heres what we offer: Comprehensive health insurance to ensure your well-being. Enjoy the peace of mind with 100% paid sick leaves. Fuel your professional growth with access to extra education opportunities. Recharge and relax with a generous 20 working days of paid vacation and additional days off. We've got your back if youre ready to relocate receive full support throughout the process. Be part of a vibrant international team united by a shared passion for excellence in product development. Enhance your language skills with language courses tailored to your needs. Unleash your inner adventurer with